      <div type="clause" n="42">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 42</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="256" ed="#liebermann"/>K. Eac we [gyt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VIAtr_42.lnote.oe.2"/>] willað myngian [georne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VIAtr_42.lnote.oe.2"/>] freonda gehwilcne, ealswa us neod is gelome to donne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> gehwa hine sylfne georne beþence,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete"><pb n="256" ed="#liebermann"/>And git we willað myngian freonda gehwilcne, ealswa us neod is gelome to donne, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#VIAtr_42.lnote.oe.star2"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> gehwa hine silfne georne beþence,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="42[a]" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="104" ed="#robertson"/>Eac we<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_42.robnote.fn.1"/> gyt willað myngian georne<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VIAtr_42.robnote.fn.2"/> freonda gehwilcne, ealswa us neod is gelome to donne, þæt gehwa hine sylfne georne beþence,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="174" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Eac we gyt willað myngian georne freonda gehwilcne, ealswa us neod is gelome to donne, þæt gehwa hine sylfne georne beþence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="257" ed="#liebermann"/>Auch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_42.lnote.de.1"/> (Und noch <hi rend="italic">D</hi>) wollen wir dèr Freunde jeden (eifrig <hi rend="italic">K</hi>) ermahnen, wie häufig zu thun uns nöthig ist, dass jeder eifrig auf sich selbst achte</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Also (And further, D) we will (eagerly, K) exhort each of our friends, as we often need to do, that everyone take careful heed of himself</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="105" ed="#robertson"/>And likewise we desire earnestly to exhort all our friends<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_42.robnote.n.1"/>, as there is need for us to do frequently, to take thought diligently for themselves,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="175" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Moreover, we also earnestly desire to admonish each of our friends, just as there is often need for us to do, to sincerely give thought to themselves.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_43-1">VIII Atr 43.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="334"><label>recurs in later code</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-069">Cn 1018 28–36</ref> <quote>Almost all these additions recurred in codes later drafted by Wulfstan for Cnut (n. 332: VI Atr 42–49, Cn 1018 28–36)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="346"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-069">Cn 1018 28–36</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-069">Cn 1018 28–36</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">D's ‘⁊’ before ‘þæt gehwa’ should be struck.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gyt: added in Wulfstan’s handwriting K</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">georne: added in Wulfstan’s handwriting K</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIAtr_42.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">256</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above late</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIAtr_42.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">256</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zu streichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be deleted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_42.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">177</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">42—49 steht in <hi rend="italic">Sermo Lupi</hi> (Wulfstan) ed. Napier 308f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">42—49 occur in the <hi rend="italic">Sermo Lupi</hi> (Wulfstan) ed. Napier 308f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_42.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. 6; 28.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIAtr_42.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><label>we</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">And git we</hi> D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIAtr_42.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><label>georne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. D.</seg></note>
      </div>
